{
  "doc": "Shared parity fixture for resolveSlots / resolve_slots (task 050) AND canonicalMapViewport / canonical_map_viewport (multiplier-model rewrite — see MAP_RENDERING_PLAN.md §'The lever model'). The TS test (src/lib/__tests__/layout.test.ts) and the Rust test (src-tauri/tests/layout_parity.rs) both load this file and assert that their port produces the listed `expected` output for `resolve_slots` AND the listed `expected_canonical_map_viewport` for `canonical_map_viewport(aspect, map_slot.w, map_slot.h, resolution)`. Under the multiplier model: multiplier = output_dims(aspect, resolution).w / output_dims(aspect, '1080p').w; css_w = round(slot_w / multiplier); css_h = round(slot_h / multiplier); pixel_ratio = multiplier. Cases without an explicit `resolution` default to 1080p (multiplier = 1, css_w = slot_w, css_h = slot_h, pixel_ratio = 1.0). Adding a new case is one PR touching one file; both ports pick it up automatically. Float `pixel_ratio` values must be compared with an epsilon tolerance (~1e-9 in Rust, toBeCloseTo(_, 9) in TS); css_w / css_h are integers and assert exactly.",
